WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:01.170
- I don't think it's that hard.

00:00:01.170 --> 00:00:02.120
I think all you have to do is

00:00:02.120 --> 00:00:03.720
feed them twice a day.

00:00:03.720 --> 00:00:04.777
I don't know,

00:00:04.777 --> 00:00:05.610
you water them.

00:00:05.610 --> 00:00:06.590
Is that all you do with babies?

00:00:06.590 --> 00:00:09.994
(baby screaming)

00:00:09.994 --> 00:00:11.327
It will be okay.

00:00:13.229 --> 00:00:15.812
(upbeat music)

00:00:18.180 --> 00:00:19.013
Babies,

00:00:19.013 --> 00:00:19.846
who needs them?

00:00:21.270 --> 00:00:22.550
- Okay, whatever, sure.

00:00:22.550 --> 00:00:25.030
Technically, we, like, need babies

00:00:25.030 --> 00:00:26.550
To continue society.

00:00:26.550 --> 00:00:28.300
Babies are super expensive,

00:00:28.300 --> 00:00:29.520
they're very needy,

00:00:29.520 --> 00:00:30.450
they're mean.

00:00:30.450 --> 00:00:31.673
Sure, they're cute and all but,

00:00:31.673 --> 00:00:33.580
they're kind of hard to work with.

00:00:33.580 --> 00:00:34.910
What is it like to be a parent?

00:00:34.910 --> 00:00:36.520
- I've always wanted to be a mom

00:00:36.520 --> 00:00:38.350
and I just get the opportunity

00:00:38.350 --> 00:00:41.050
to have someone, and
raise her and love her

00:00:41.050 --> 00:00:42.580
and pour everything into her.

00:00:42.580 --> 00:00:43.930
- The one thing that
makes me nervous about it,

00:00:43.930 --> 00:00:45.620
are some of the challenges.

00:00:45.620 --> 00:00:46.610
Babies throw tantrums.

00:00:46.610 --> 00:00:48.410
- So, Sydney, she's 20 months now

00:00:48.410 --> 00:00:50.160
and she's very independent.

00:00:50.160 --> 00:00:52.810
She's really trying to find her way

00:00:52.810 --> 00:00:54.020
around the world.

00:00:54.020 --> 00:00:55.670
She can't fully articulate

00:00:55.670 --> 00:00:57.400
what she wants a little bit,

00:00:57.400 --> 00:00:58.430
but when she can't,

00:00:58.430 --> 00:00:59.263
she cries.

00:00:59.263 --> 00:01:00.096
Babies will let you know

00:01:00.096 --> 00:01:01.220
when something isn't right.

00:01:01.220 --> 00:01:02.737
- What do you think I'm
going to struggle with?

00:01:02.737 --> 00:01:04.040
- I think in the very beginning,

00:01:04.040 --> 00:01:04.930
when I'm leaving,

00:01:04.930 --> 00:01:06.520
she may wonder "where's mom?"

00:01:06.520 --> 00:01:07.883
and she may cry around that time.

00:01:07.883 --> 00:01:09.220
You know, you take the good

00:01:09.220 --> 00:01:10.413
with the not so great and,

00:01:10.413 --> 00:01:12.050
you just kind of roll with it.

00:01:12.050 --> 00:01:13.714
I think the rewards far outweigh

00:01:13.714 --> 00:01:15.350
the things that are stressful.

00:01:15.350 --> 00:01:16.183
- Shaniqua going already.

00:01:16.183 --> 00:01:17.016
- Yes, are you ready?

00:01:18.890 --> 00:01:19.723
- I think so.

00:01:19.723 --> 00:01:20.740
I get to leave work early

00:01:20.740 --> 00:01:22.300
so that's a plus.

00:01:22.300 --> 00:01:23.470
- You leave one job to go

00:01:23.470 --> 00:01:24.540
to another job,

00:01:24.540 --> 00:01:25.590
practice being a dad.

00:01:27.964 --> 00:01:30.140
- Okay, well, any advice

00:01:30.140 --> 00:01:31.096
before I do this?

00:01:31.096 --> 00:01:32.380
- Just, you know,

00:01:32.380 --> 00:01:33.770
it's not a sprint, it's a marathon.

00:01:33.770 --> 00:01:34.603
- Okay.

00:01:35.950 --> 00:01:37.283
Alright, so we just got Sydney.

00:01:37.283 --> 00:01:39.081
Can you say hi, Sydney?

00:01:39.081 --> 00:01:39.914
- Say hi, Sydney.

00:01:39.914 --> 00:01:40.747
- Hi.

00:01:40.747 --> 00:01:43.210
She's not interested in saying hi now,

00:01:43.210 --> 00:01:44.043
but we're going to get her in the

00:01:44.043 --> 00:01:45.380
car seat here.

00:01:45.380 --> 00:01:46.580
- She may just drop in and sit

00:01:46.580 --> 00:01:48.190
and be all compliant,

00:01:48.190 --> 00:01:49.474
other times she is going to stand

00:01:49.474 --> 00:01:50.880
and not want to sit.

00:01:50.880 --> 00:01:52.540
It will take some time
to get her in there.

00:01:52.540 --> 00:01:54.740
- I was expecting her to be very frantic

00:01:54.740 --> 00:01:56.250
because Shaniqua warned me that there

00:01:56.250 --> 00:01:57.130
would be tantrums,

00:01:57.130 --> 00:01:58.110
but it was super easy.

00:01:58.110 --> 00:01:59.380
Sydney was very docile.

00:01:59.380 --> 00:02:00.250
She was adorable.

00:02:00.250 --> 00:02:01.390
She was super sweet.

00:02:01.390 --> 00:02:03.470
I put her in the car, it was no big deal,

00:02:03.470 --> 00:02:04.420
she got in...

00:02:04.420 --> 00:02:06.120
Now we're going to go grocery shopping.

00:02:06.120 --> 00:02:07.560
Okay.

00:02:07.560 --> 00:02:08.690
She hopped in the cart,

00:02:08.690 --> 00:02:09.600
it was super simple.

00:02:09.600 --> 00:02:11.120
We were walking around.

00:02:11.120 --> 00:02:12.258
We're going to go grocery shopping

00:02:12.258 --> 00:02:13.380
You got it?

00:02:13.380 --> 00:02:14.740
You okay?

00:02:14.740 --> 00:02:16.790
So, Shaniqua got me this

00:02:16.790 --> 00:02:18.220
handy dandy grocery list.

00:02:18.220 --> 00:02:19.316
Sydney is being very good

00:02:19.316 --> 00:02:21.630
and this is so far, so good.

00:02:21.630 --> 00:02:22.950
She was a great helper.

00:02:22.950 --> 00:02:24.160
Any time I handed her an item

00:02:24.160 --> 00:02:26.060
she put it right back
in the basket for me.

00:02:26.060 --> 00:02:27.316
She was the best.

00:02:27.316 --> 00:02:29.170
Do you like the raspberries?

00:02:29.170 --> 00:02:30.003
Yes?

00:02:30.003 --> 00:02:30.953
Awesome!

00:02:32.080 --> 00:02:33.219
Good job, Sydney.

00:02:33.219 --> 00:02:34.913
Do you like the mangoes?

00:02:34.913 --> 00:02:36.471
Yeah?

00:02:36.471 --> 00:02:37.421
Want to toss it in?

00:02:39.197 --> 00:02:42.283
Good job! Alright!

00:02:43.690 --> 00:02:44.523
Going into this,

00:02:44.523 --> 00:02:46.120
I was like, I am not a baby person.

00:02:46.120 --> 00:02:47.560
I think that they are very difficult,

00:02:47.560 --> 00:02:49.170
but, this first hour with Sydney

00:02:49.170 --> 00:02:50.003
was amazing.

00:02:50.003 --> 00:02:50.836
I felt like,

00:02:50.836 --> 00:02:52.546
I am the best dad in the world.

00:02:52.546 --> 00:02:54.180
Then I tried to put her in the car

00:02:54.180 --> 00:02:55.240
after the grocery store

00:02:55.240 --> 00:02:56.900
and we had tantrum number one.

00:02:56.900 --> 00:02:59.214
Okay, so we just left the grocery store.

00:02:59.214 --> 00:03:00.410
(baby whining)

00:03:00.410 --> 00:03:01.810
Sydney, it will be okay.

00:03:01.810 --> 00:03:02.750
She's a little anxious,

00:03:02.750 --> 00:03:03.967
I think she's ready to eat.

00:03:03.967 --> 00:03:05.940
Alright, oh wait,

00:03:05.940 --> 00:03:07.240
no, wait,

00:03:07.240 --> 00:03:08.315
Sydney, you can't stand.

00:03:08.315 --> 00:03:09.382
Wait, Sydney.

00:03:09.382 --> 00:03:10.215
(baby cries)

00:03:10.215 --> 00:03:12.010
Sydney, I know.

00:03:12.010 --> 00:03:13.712
I know, but we have to get in the seat.

00:03:13.712 --> 00:03:16.340
(baby wailing)
Oh no,

00:03:16.340 --> 00:03:17.173
oh my gosh.

00:03:17.173 --> 00:03:18.006
Okay, Sydney,

00:03:18.006 --> 00:03:19.096
I know.

00:03:19.096 --> 00:03:20.540
We're going to have some snacks.

00:03:20.540 --> 00:03:21.424
We're going to have snacks, okay?

00:03:21.424 --> 00:03:23.529
(baby crying loudly)

00:03:23.529 --> 00:03:25.446
I know, I know, I know.

00:03:26.370 --> 00:03:27.770
She just started screaming and,

00:03:27.770 --> 00:03:29.130
I couldn't get her in the car.

00:03:29.130 --> 00:03:30.750
She was kicking to try to get back,

00:03:30.750 --> 00:03:31.966
like, I don't know what happened.

00:03:31.966 --> 00:03:33.900
Sydney was just not having it,

00:03:33.900 --> 00:03:36.510
And I was, like, we've
been together for two hours

00:03:36.510 --> 00:03:38.396
and you're already doing the most...

00:03:38.396 --> 00:03:40.159
Do you want a snack?

00:03:40.159 --> 00:03:41.926
(baby screaming)

00:03:41.926 --> 00:03:43.536
I had no idea what I was doing.

00:03:43.536 --> 00:03:45.470
It's very frustrating,

00:03:45.470 --> 00:03:47.040
because they can't communicate with you

00:03:47.040 --> 00:03:48.130
so they're frustrated.

00:03:48.130 --> 00:03:49.124
You can't communicate with them

00:03:49.124 --> 00:03:50.410
so you're frustrated.

00:03:50.410 --> 00:03:53.020
This was the first challenge
where I didn't know what to do

00:03:53.020 --> 00:03:54.380
and I was like, oh,

00:03:54.380 --> 00:03:56.042
this is going to be quite the battle.

00:03:56.042 --> 00:03:57.600
We're just now getting home,

00:03:57.600 --> 00:03:58.535
Sydney, can we...

00:03:58.535 --> 00:03:59.368
(baby crying)

00:03:59.368 --> 00:04:00.251
can we go inside?

00:04:00.251 --> 00:04:01.362
No? Okay.

00:04:01.362 --> 00:04:03.890
Yep, this is tantrum two,

00:04:03.890 --> 00:04:05.030
but it will be okay.

00:04:05.030 --> 00:04:05.983
It will be okay, Sydney.

00:04:05.983 --> 00:04:08.073
Sydney, we're going to wash our hands.

00:04:08.073 --> 00:04:09.844
We're going to grab some soap,

00:04:09.844 --> 00:04:11.220
(baby whimpers)

00:04:11.220 --> 00:04:12.584
it's okay.

00:04:12.584 --> 00:04:14.319
(baby cries loudly)

00:04:14.319 --> 00:04:15.398
Can I have...

00:04:15.398 --> 00:04:16.924
we're going to eat though.

00:04:16.924 --> 00:04:17.930
(baby sobs)

00:04:17.930 --> 00:04:19.580
I know, Sydney, it will be okay.

00:04:19.580 --> 00:04:21.035
(baby screams)

00:04:21.035 --> 00:04:22.041
I know,

00:04:22.041 --> 00:04:24.124
I know, but can I wash...

00:04:29.323 --> 00:04:31.223
I sit down and eat dinner with Sydney.

00:04:32.150 --> 00:04:33.461
You want to start with the grapes?

00:04:33.461 --> 00:04:34.398
That's okay.

00:04:34.398 --> 00:04:35.887
It's okay.

00:04:35.887 --> 00:04:37.910
I'm going to get some strawberries

00:04:37.910 --> 00:04:39.219
ready for you, okay?

00:04:39.219 --> 00:04:40.420
Enjoy it.

00:04:40.420 --> 00:04:42.323
Let me know if you need anything.

00:04:44.070 --> 00:04:45.630
Things move very quickly
when you have a baby.

00:04:45.630 --> 00:04:47.110
Toddlers they,

00:04:47.110 --> 00:04:49.110
okay, okay, she needs me now.

00:04:49.110 --> 00:04:49.943
Here we go.

00:04:49.943 --> 00:04:52.872
Just had a little spill?

00:04:52.872 --> 00:04:54.323
Say thank you?

00:04:57.270 --> 00:04:59.310
I didn't realize how much of a mess

00:04:59.310 --> 00:05:00.380
babies would be.

00:05:00.380 --> 00:05:02.500
She just kind of kept putting
her fingers in everything

00:05:02.500 --> 00:05:04.040
and taking it off of her plate,

00:05:04.040 --> 00:05:05.200
throwing it on the ground.

00:05:05.200 --> 00:05:06.899
This is where I'm leaning
back on the meter of,

00:05:06.899 --> 00:05:08.348
I don't think kids are for me.

00:05:08.348 --> 00:05:09.882
This getting ready for bedtime is

00:05:09.882 --> 00:05:11.255
around 7:45?

00:05:11.255 --> 00:05:12.088
- Yes.

00:05:12.088 --> 00:05:12.921
- It's hard for me to go to sleep so,

00:05:12.921 --> 00:05:14.319
I can only imagine a child,

00:05:14.319 --> 00:05:15.152
- Right, right.

00:05:15.152 --> 00:05:16.177
- Being like, no, I'm not doing this,

00:05:16.177 --> 00:05:17.340
especially at 8:30,

00:05:17.340 --> 00:05:18.173
that seems so early.

00:05:18.173 --> 00:05:19.640
- I mean, it's early when you think about

00:05:19.640 --> 00:05:21.010
all the other things you need to do.

00:05:21.010 --> 00:05:21.950
Because at this point,

00:05:21.950 --> 00:05:22.783
I've given you a list.

00:05:22.783 --> 00:05:24.680
You haven't shared anything about you,

00:05:24.680 --> 00:05:27.220
you haven't even gone to the bathroom yet.

00:05:27.220 --> 00:05:28.053
- By this point,

00:05:28.053 --> 00:05:30.840
it's about 7:00 and
Sydney is full of energy.

00:05:30.840 --> 00:05:32.930
She wants to run around and play games.

00:05:32.930 --> 00:05:34.879
We sat down and had an adorable moment.

00:05:34.879 --> 00:05:36.670
We had tea parties.

00:05:36.670 --> 00:05:37.750
We read books.

00:05:37.750 --> 00:05:39.266
We played with several different dolls,

00:05:39.266 --> 00:05:41.330
but it was exhausting.

00:05:41.330 --> 00:05:42.440
They're not letting up at all.

00:05:42.440 --> 00:05:44.520
Sydney has so much energy,

00:05:44.520 --> 00:05:46.170
she would play with a toy for two seconds,

00:05:46.170 --> 00:05:47.003
run over here and jump

00:05:47.003 --> 00:05:48.030
on the trampoline for two seconds,

00:05:48.030 --> 00:05:49.210
run into her room,

00:05:49.210 --> 00:05:51.750
and it was just like she
was all over the place.

00:05:51.750 --> 00:05:53.251
By this point, it's 8:30 and I've done,

00:05:53.251 --> 00:05:54.659
literally nothing for myself.

00:05:54.659 --> 00:05:56.010
You're tired,

00:05:56.010 --> 00:05:57.020
She's clearly tired,

00:05:57.020 --> 00:05:58.140
but she doesn't want to go to bed

00:05:58.140 --> 00:05:59.150
and it's just, like,

00:05:59.150 --> 00:06:00.900
the most frustrating thing in the world.

00:06:00.900 --> 00:06:02.467
Alright, Sydney, ready to get dressed?

00:06:02.467 --> 00:06:03.381
- Dressed!

00:06:03.381 --> 00:06:06.080
- Let's do this.

00:06:06.080 --> 00:06:07.860
Finally, Shaniqua has
to come help me again

00:06:07.860 --> 00:06:10.330
to get Sydney into her bed because,

00:06:10.330 --> 00:06:11.680
she was not having it.

00:06:11.680 --> 00:06:13.620
But, then I still have to clean
up the dishes from Sydney.

00:06:13.620 --> 00:06:15.210
I still have to make sure her meals

00:06:15.210 --> 00:06:16.590
are ready for the next day.

00:06:16.590 --> 00:06:19.053
I still have to get all
of her clothes ready,

00:06:19.053 --> 00:06:21.870
and I'm just, like, this is hard.

00:06:21.870 --> 00:06:23.273
It's so hard.

00:06:25.526 --> 00:06:26.570
(alarm beeps)

00:06:26.570 --> 00:06:28.980
I set an alarm for six o'clock,

00:06:28.980 --> 00:06:30.500
because I knew that
Sydney usually wakes up

00:06:30.500 --> 00:06:32.139
between 6:30 and 7:00.

00:06:32.139 --> 00:06:34.840
I wake up and I don't hear Sydney crying,

00:06:34.840 --> 00:06:36.260
so I'm like, perfect,

00:06:36.260 --> 00:06:37.093
fine,

00:06:37.093 --> 00:06:38.080
I'm going to go back to sleep

00:06:38.080 --> 00:06:39.910
and then I sleep through my second alarm

00:06:39.910 --> 00:06:42.960
and then I wake up and
Sydney is ready to go.

00:06:42.960 --> 00:06:43.910
She's ready for breakfast.

00:06:43.910 --> 00:06:44.743
She's hungry.

00:06:44.743 --> 00:06:45.576
She's running around.

00:06:45.576 --> 00:06:46.409
She has tons of energy,

00:06:46.409 --> 00:06:47.810
and I am like, how are we doing this?

00:06:47.810 --> 00:06:48.930
It's Saturday.

00:06:48.930 --> 00:06:50.750
All I want to do is be in my bed

00:06:50.750 --> 00:06:51.715
and asleep until 3:00.

00:06:51.715 --> 00:06:53.748
Woke up a little bit late for breakfast,

00:06:53.748 --> 00:06:56.790
I started to make waffles

00:06:56.790 --> 00:06:59.696
but didn't plug in the oven.

00:06:59.696 --> 00:07:01.110
Good start.

00:07:01.110 --> 00:07:02.629
We get Sydney's breakfast together.

00:07:02.629 --> 00:07:04.275
We just cut up food.

00:07:04.275 --> 00:07:06.478
I didn't realize how much babies eat,

00:07:06.478 --> 00:07:08.167
like Sydney was just going at it

00:07:08.167 --> 00:07:09.270
and then she was like, more,

00:07:09.270 --> 00:07:10.640
more strawberries.

00:07:10.640 --> 00:07:11.915
You just have to constantly keep going,

00:07:11.915 --> 00:07:13.318
and keep thinking ahead.

00:07:13.318 --> 00:07:14.880
We got breakfast started.

00:07:14.880 --> 00:07:16.172
It looks like it's going well.

00:07:16.172 --> 00:07:18.843
Did you drop these plates and the cup?

00:07:21.790 --> 00:07:22.940
Why are you doing that?

00:07:23.950 --> 00:07:25.540
One area that I really enjoyed

00:07:25.540 --> 00:07:26.810
about being a dad for a day,

00:07:26.810 --> 00:07:28.810
was getting to pick out Sydney's outfits.

00:07:28.810 --> 00:07:30.870
I'm thinking like having
her like North West.

00:07:30.870 --> 00:07:32.800
I want her to look like little Blue Ivy.

00:07:32.800 --> 00:07:34.987
I am super excited to
pick out her clothes,

00:07:34.987 --> 00:07:37.052
but I didn't think about
the weather at first

00:07:37.052 --> 00:07:38.499
so I pick out t-shirts

00:07:38.499 --> 00:07:42.030
and Shaniqua is like, "No,
you can't put her in t-shirts,

00:07:42.030 --> 00:07:43.260
it's going to be 50 degrees tomorrow."

00:07:43.260 --> 00:07:44.910
I forgot weather, and babies have

00:07:46.110 --> 00:07:47.110
sensitivity to cold.

00:07:48.390 --> 00:07:50.350
Okay, Sydney, it's time for music class

00:07:50.350 --> 00:07:52.640
so we're going to take this so we can...

00:07:52.640 --> 00:07:53.548
I know, I know.

00:07:53.548 --> 00:07:55.047
But you can learn to dance and sing,

00:07:55.047 --> 00:07:57.250
so we're going to turn this off for now.

00:07:57.250 --> 00:07:58.264
Ready? Ready?

00:07:58.264 --> 00:08:01.473
Okay, we're going to music class.

00:08:01.473 --> 00:08:03.553
Sydney, do you want to play?

00:08:06.980 --> 00:08:07.849
- [Woman] Pull and then you let go.

00:08:07.849 --> 00:08:09.056
(banging on drum)

00:08:09.056 --> 00:08:12.370
- [Man] I see you're
playing, Sydney, I see.

00:08:12.370 --> 00:08:13.203
- Thank you.

00:08:14.146 --> 00:08:16.313
(giggles)

00:08:17.428 --> 00:08:19.345
- Want to get the door?

00:08:20.600 --> 00:08:22.330
Sydney falls asleep on the way back

00:08:22.330 --> 00:08:23.400
from music class

00:08:23.400 --> 00:08:24.990
and I just pick her up out of the car seat

00:08:24.990 --> 00:08:26.670
and we have this really precious moment.

00:08:26.670 --> 00:08:28.560
Oh, wait, nap time for one to two hours.

00:08:28.560 --> 00:08:29.930
- Yes.
- Great, so I get a nap.

00:08:29.930 --> 00:08:30.950
- [Woman] You should, yeah.

00:08:30.950 --> 00:08:31.783
You should.

00:08:31.783 --> 00:08:33.370
- You keep saying should.
- Yeah, because you

00:08:33.370 --> 00:08:34.203
just never know.

00:08:34.203 --> 00:08:35.036
You just have to be prepared

00:08:35.036 --> 00:08:37.010
and don't bank on something happening

00:08:37.010 --> 00:08:38.863
because it's very fluid.

00:08:48.806 --> 00:08:49.639
It ended up being a mistake,

00:08:49.639 --> 00:08:51.540
because Sydney wakes up 30 minutes later

00:08:51.540 --> 00:08:53.300
and she's ready to eat.

00:08:53.300 --> 00:08:55.150
She's like, "Where's my food?"

00:08:55.150 --> 00:08:55.983
We woke up from a nap

00:08:55.983 --> 00:08:57.920
and now we're going to
have a little lunch.

00:08:57.920 --> 00:08:59.310
We had a little mini-nap,

00:08:59.310 --> 00:09:00.340
so we're going to have to take another,

00:09:00.340 --> 00:09:01.600
longer nap after this.

00:09:01.600 --> 00:09:03.450
Are you okay for nap time after this?

00:09:04.560 --> 00:09:05.763
No, you're busy eating,

00:09:05.763 --> 00:09:06.769
I don't know why I am talking to you

00:09:06.769 --> 00:09:07.602
while you're eating.

00:09:07.602 --> 00:09:09.700
Eating with Sydney is always an adventure.

00:09:09.700 --> 00:09:11.200
All of her food wound up either

00:09:11.200 --> 00:09:13.495
on her body or on the floor.

00:09:13.495 --> 00:09:15.340
I hang out with Sydney for a little bit

00:09:15.340 --> 00:09:16.540
and I keep trying to get her to go

00:09:16.540 --> 00:09:17.690
back down for a nap.

00:09:17.690 --> 00:09:18.890
I want Sydney to nap,

00:09:18.890 --> 00:09:20.350
so I can nap,

00:09:20.350 --> 00:09:21.530
but she's not giving me

00:09:21.530 --> 00:09:22.650
any type of a break.

00:09:22.650 --> 00:09:23.730
Since she didn't want to go to nap,

00:09:23.730 --> 00:09:25.490
we just went to the park.

00:09:25.490 --> 00:09:26.490
That's probably my favorite part.

00:09:26.490 --> 00:09:27.323
Hang out with a toddler for 24 hours

00:09:27.323 --> 00:09:29.530
and you really get to see
how they see the world.

00:09:29.530 --> 00:09:30.800
It was little moments like that,

00:09:30.800 --> 00:09:32.958
it started to sit in in
the last couple of hours.

00:09:32.958 --> 00:09:35.652
It was like, this is the
fun part of being a parent.

00:09:35.652 --> 00:09:39.980
You get to relive your
childhood through someone else.

00:09:39.980 --> 00:09:42.310
You get to see how smart, and talented,

00:09:42.310 --> 00:09:44.240
and cool your toddler is.

00:09:44.240 --> 00:09:45.373
Where's Sydney?

00:09:46.679 --> 00:09:47.948
Whoa!

00:09:47.948 --> 00:09:50.420
- There are times where
things will be easy and fun.

00:09:50.420 --> 00:09:52.380
There are times when things
will be a bit challenging.

00:09:52.380 --> 00:09:53.774
You take the good with the not so great

00:09:53.774 --> 00:09:55.810
and you just kind of roll with it.

00:09:55.810 --> 00:09:57.386
I think the rewards far outweigh

00:09:57.386 --> 00:09:59.170
the things that are stressful.

00:09:59.170 --> 00:10:00.281
- Here we go.

00:10:00.281 --> 00:10:02.840
This is so much easier than last time.

00:10:02.840 --> 00:10:03.860
This is a major improvement.

00:10:03.860 --> 00:10:05.380
I'm not that much of a planner

00:10:05.380 --> 00:10:08.300
so, it's really hard to deal with a kid

00:10:08.300 --> 00:10:09.970
who just completely needs you.

00:10:09.970 --> 00:10:11.610
And you have to think about
all the things they need,

00:10:11.610 --> 00:10:12.921
on top of all the things you need.

00:10:12.921 --> 00:10:15.510
It made me appreciate growing up so much,

00:10:15.510 --> 00:10:17.626
and all the sacrifices my mom made for me.

00:10:17.626 --> 00:10:19.950
It's a tough job and there are a lot

00:10:19.950 --> 00:10:21.210
of people out there that want to do it,

00:10:21.210 --> 00:10:22.802
I just don't happen to be one of them.

00:10:22.802 --> 00:10:25.385
(upbeat music)

00:10:34.297 --> 00:10:35.703
High five, maybe?

00:10:35.703 --> 00:10:36.536
Alright!

